          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "চাখা (chākhā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from cakṣati, \"tastes\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 4557). CDIAL lists Bengali cākhā, \"to taste\"."
